# and `--exact` matches: a test of this directory by its function name, as it is written after
# `fn`; a unit test of a library by its path in that library (`module::tests::name`). `#` starts a
# comment, and blank lines are skipped.
#
# Who reads it: the gate's test step, scripts/test_step.sh (the step `test` of ci.yml's job `gate`
# and of scripts/ci_local.sh, and the step `test on macOS` of the job `macos`). It runs the
# workspace's tests with these names skipped, then these names alone, one at a time
# (`--test-threads=1`): every name here runs in every gate. The mutation driver does not read it
# yet (it is to pass them as `--skip` filters and to rerun alone a mutant that only they caught).
#
# How a name gets on it: a failure of the test that is not of the code, recorded with the run that
# showed it (a command and its log) and its cause, while the test passes on the same tree
# otherwise; it comes off by a measurement that the cause is gone. A name that is here because
# the code is slow is a finding about the code, not an entry. The test
# `the_load_sensitive_list_names_tests_that_exist` (in agent_hook.rs) fails when a name here is
# no test function of this directory or of the library its path names, or is here twice.
